  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A powerful magnet of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.5\\text{ kg}\"></span> is held fixed above a steel nail of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.010\\text{ kg}\"></span>. The nail is released from rest and accelerates upwards at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"15\\text{ m s}^{-2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>During this motion, the magnet exerts a force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{mag}}\"></span> on the nail and the nail exerts a force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{nail}}\"></span> on the magnet. Which of the following correctly relates the magnitudes of these forces? (Assume <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"g = 9.8\\text{ m s}^{-2}\"></span>)</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{mag}} = 0.248\\text{ N}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{nail}} &lt; F_{\\text{mag}}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{mag}} = 0.248\\text{ N}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{nail}} = F_{\\text{mag}}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{mag}} = 0.150\\text{ N}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{nail}} = F_{\\text{mag}}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{mag}} = 0.150\\text{ N}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{nail}} &lt; F_{\\text{mag}}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
